{
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "status": "supported",
      "witness": null,
      "reason": "The calibrated probability of default (p1) is 0.0511, which rounds to 5.1%. The target definition and horizon match the claim: default payment due after the September 2005 statement (next month)."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "status": "supported",
      "witness": null,
      "reason": "The model attributes negative contributions (decreases risk) to all six PAY_* fields (f4–f9), each with value -1.0 (paid duly), and the derived pay_max (f3) also has a negative attribution. The claim correctly states that consistent on-time payments lower the risk score, and the time period (April–September 2005) is fully supported by the evidence."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "status": "supported",
      "witness": null,
      "reason": "The amounts NT$25,413 (PAY_AMT2, f1), NT$75,459 (PAY_AMT1, f2), and NT$85,784 (PAY_AMT3, f10) are all correctly stated and match the evidence. Each has a negative attribution (a1, a2, a4) indicating they decrease risk. The claim is a plain-language restatement of the evidence and does not violate any contract rules. The 'binding not established' note refers to field name ambiguity, but the values and attributions are unambiguously matched."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c4",
      "status": "supported",
      "witness": null,
      "reason": "The model's base value (shap_base_value) is -1.05291, and the raw margin for this borrower is -4.193, which is substantially lower (more favorable). Since lower log-odds correspond to lower risk, this borrower's risk score is indeed lower than the average (expected) borrower in the training fold. The claim is a valid interpretation of the model's reference background and does not assert causation or misrepresent the scale."
    }
  ],
  "omissions": []
}

